-- Post-migration snapshot of the demo dataset.
--
-- WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: this repo syncs Oracle -> Adabas, so it needs rows in
-- Oracle to change. In the real flow those rows arrive from the sibling
-- adabas-to-oracle-migration repo's bulk load. Committing the result here keeps
-- this repo runnable on its own, without the migration repo present.
--
-- GENERATED, NOT HAND-WRITTEN. It is a dump of the sibling lab's POCAPP schema
-- taken after a successful migrate.cmd run. Regenerate it rather than editing
-- it: run the migration lab, then dump POCAPP in the same statement order.
-- 01_schema.sql and 02_lookups.sql are byte-identical copies of that repo's
-- files, so the two labs cannot drift apart in the model.
--
-- IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT SEED THE IDENTITY COLUMNS. vehicle_id, fine_id and
-- reject_id are GENERATED ALWAYS AS IDENTITY, so an explicit insert raises
-- ORA-32795 - and forcing one would strand the identity sequence at 1, so the
-- first INSERT a test performs would collide on the primary key. Instead the
-- identity assigns the key naturally and every child row resolves its parent
-- through the natural key: vin for a vehicle, fine_no for a fine. Both carry a
-- UNIQUE constraint. No DDL, no ALTER, no divergence from the sibling schema.
--
-- Runs automatically on FIRST container start only
-- (/container-entrypoint-initdb.d). Each init script gets its own sqlplus
-- session against the CDB root, hence the ALTER SESSION below.
--
-- Rows: 773 vehicles, 797 plates, 1136 fines, 2271 offences, 682 payments,
-- 31 migration rejects. The lookup tables are seeded by 02_lookups.sql.
--
-- Source: Software AG Adabas Community Edition demo data, in its migrated
-- relational form. See the README licence note.

ALTER SESSION SET CONTAINER = FREEPDB1;
SET DEFINE OFF;

PROMPT seeding VEHICLE ...
PROMPT seeding VEHICLE_PLATE ...
PROMPT seeding TRAFFIC_FINE ...
PROMPT seeding TRAFFIC_FINE_OFFENCE ...
PROMPT seeding TRAFFIC_FINE_PAYMENT ...
PROMPT seeding MIGRATION_REJECT ...

COMMIT;
EXIT;
